<%= content_for :title, "Generation Status" %>

<%#
  #13 Turbo Stream subscription — subscribes this page to live updates from
  the generation loop.  Broadcasts targeting this GenerationRequest will be
  delivered via Action Cable to all subscribers on this stream.
%>
<%= turbo_stream_from @generation_request %>

<%# group/genlog = the named :has() scope for the Generation log's terminal-state
    release. Named (not the bare `group`) so it can never be triggered by another
    .group elsewhere — the layout header's logo link uses an unnamed group too.
    Once the status partial below swaps in its data-generation-finished panel
    (succeeded / failed), the group-has-*/genlog variants further down drop the
    log's bounded scroll height so the finished record flows as a normal,
    page-scrolled document. Driven entirely in CSS off that sentinel — no extra
    broadcast, no re-render of the streamed entries, so there is no completion
    flicker. %>
<div class="group/genlog mx-auto flex w-full min-h-0 max-w-3xl flex-1 flex-col space-y-8">
  <header>
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-content-strong">Generation status</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-content-muted">error-as-feedback loop · what you verify is what ships</p>
  </header>

  <section class="border border-edge-default bg-surface-raised p-5">
    <p class="mb-1 text-sm font-medium text-content-muted">Requirement</p>
    <p class="text-content-default"><%= @generation_request.requirement %></p>
  </section>

  <%#
    Status panel. The frame inside is updated by two paths: a live Turbo Stream
    broadcast (GenerationRequest#broadcast_status_to_self — instant, happy path)
    and the status-reconciler controller polling EndpointsController#status. The
    reconciler closes the Action Cable subscribe race: a run can finish before
    the browser subscribes (e.g. an instant LLM failure), and Action Cable does
    not replay the missed broadcast — so the panel would stay stuck on
    "Generating…". finished-value seeds the controller so an already-terminal run
    is never polled.
  %>
  <div data-controller="status-reconciler"
       data-status-reconciler-url-value="<%= status_endpoint_path(@generation_request) %>"
       data-status-reconciler-finished-value="<%= !@generation_request.pending? %>">
    <%= render "status_frame", generation_request: @generation_request %>
  </div>

  <%#
    Generation log — each Message (LLM turn / tool call result) is appended here
    in real time by Message#broadcast_message_to_generation_request as the agent
    runs.  Target id matches the target: kwarg in the broadcast callback.
  %>
  <%# While streaming, the section fills the remaining height so the viewport
      below can tail its own content. Once terminal (group-has the finished
      sentinel) it sheds flex-1 and sizes to content, letting the whole record
      grow and the document scroll. %>
  <section class="flex min-h-0 flex-1 flex-col gap-3 group-has-[[data-generation-finished]]/genlog:flex-none">
    <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between border-b border-edge-default pb-2">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-content-strong">Generation log</h2>
      <%# The indicator doubles as a reading cue: a live pulse while streaming,
          then a one-line caption once terminal so the audience knows the
          finished log reads top-to-bottom in the order it happened. %>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-mono text-xs text-content-muted group-has-[[data-generation-finished]]/genlog:hidden">
        <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-secondary" aria-hidden="true"></span>live
      </span>
      <span class="hidden font-mono text-xs text-content-muted group-has-[[data-generation-finished]]/genlog:inline">完整紀錄 · 由上而下為發生順序</span>
    </div>
    <%# Scroll viewport — fills the remaining viewport height (flex-1 + min-h-0)
        and tails its own content, so it adapts to any projector resolution
        without a guessed max-height. The generation-log controller keeps it
        pinned to the newest entry as Turbo Streams append into the log target.
        Once terminal it releases the bound (flex-none + overflow-visible): the
        entries stay in place but the viewport stops clipping, so the full run
        lays out top-to-bottom and the page — not this box — scrolls. %>
    <div data-controller="generation-log" class="min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-y-auto group-has-[[data-generation-finished]]/genlog:flex-none group-has-[[data-generation-finished]]/genlog:overflow-visible">
      <%# Persisted messages are rendered server-side so revisiting a finished
          run replays the full log (the live Turbo stream only fills this during
          the original generation). For an in-flight view this is safe too:
          messages persisted before load render here, and the live stream
          append/replace targets each by dom_id, so a completing message
          replaces its server-rendered placeholder rather than duplicating it.
          The target must carry NO inner whitespace so :empty still matches an
          empty log, keeping the peer placeholder below working. %>
      <div id="generation_log_<%= @generation_request.id %>" class="peer space-y-3"><%= render partial: "messages/message", collection: @generation_request.log_messages, as: :message %></div>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-content-muted peer-[:not(:empty)]:hidden">
        生成過程會即時顯示在這裡 — 每一次 LLM 改寫腳本、沙盒試跑與錯誤回饋。
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p>
    <%= link_to "← Generate another endpoint", new_endpoint_path, class: "font-mono text-sm text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:no-underline" %>
  </p>
</div>
